=====================

 S~S This Repository

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What is the purpose of the objects in this repository or repo?

    * provide an example of a self-contained moderately complex development environment

      * the transition from writing setup/loop Apps to writing RTOS or OS device drivers is a big one

      * many common data processing concepts are presented and implemented, waiting to be broken

    * There are build-time configurations with this App, and with ssTEA.  These variations are
      concerned with the debug and App and ssTEA values displayed to the user via the serial port.
      The RELEASE metadata does not describe the build/run-time changes.

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What are the contents of this repository?

   * "rr\" means "repository root\"

   * The managed object is everything, and only that, in the rr\app-fsmDemo\ directory

       * there is no rr\app-fsmDemo\SimpleSal\      (in the App repo)

          There is none because the directory rr\app-fsmDemo\App~SimpleSal
          contains all configuration files either renamed and/or modified from SimpleSal.

       * rr\app-fsmDemo\app-fsmDemo.ino             (Arduino main program)

       * app-fsmDemo.ino makes #include references to these files:

            * rr\app-fsmDemo\app_bpm_ino.h          (an App)

            * rr\app-fsmDemo\app_cmd_ssUI.h         (ssUI commands launching Apps/Events)

            * rr\app-fsmDemo\app_fifos_ino.h        (Data Events)

            * rr\app-fsmDemo\app_mrb_ino.h          (Time Events)

            * rr\app-fsmDemo\App~SimpleSal\*.*      (a variety of portability concerns)

                mesa_Select*.*          support a build on multiple Arduino mesas
                api_ssTEA_*.h           packaged API helper for ssTEA
                mesa_fsmDemo_*.h        OPTIN to replace mesa minimum functionality
                mesa_unor4wifi_LEDM.h   simple interface to LED Matrix
                mesas_min_*.h           original mesa minimum functionality if not replaced
                mesas_vocabulary.h      taking formality to the most extreme place possible
                ss_cofiguration.h       fundamental document describing SimpleSal configuration
                ss_RO_configuration.h   Co-existing software needs to take turns to resources

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What happens in my workspace as a result of interacting with this repository?

    The managed object will be placed into your workspace, along with the human metadata files
    (depending on your ability to configure the repo App to only consider files matching filters).

    The only reason to have a metadata copy locally is if files are being modified for a release.
    Readers still awake will realize the SimpleSal metadata about the directory content will
    match the name and therefore overwrite a conventional software package's local metadata files.
    This is a disadvantage resulting from TSC LLC separating the managed object into a subdirectory.

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What about the version of the SimpleSal software the App co-exists with?

    This specific version of app-time is part of a coherent SimpleSal-wide release of software.

    At a minimum, this SimpleSal App will build with any SimpleSal version
        released as or released after "V1.0.0" of 2026/10/16.

